{"id": "meta-look", "window": ["2016-10-24", "2022-12-30"], "n_touches": 60211, "sessions": 1604, "instruments": 34, "primary": "first touch of open ± 0.5σ (HAR σ), 01:00-19:00 London, entry at the touch bar's mid close; fade and follow", "intro": ["60,211 first touches of the open ± 0.5σ line on 34 instruments, 1,604 London sessions, Oct 2016 to Dec 2022 (2023 onward not loaded). Each is labelled fade and follow on six barrier shapes.", "The barriers set the hit rate, not the market. Fade 1:1 at 0.25σ with a 2-hour limit: 38.6% hit the target first; a random walk with the same barriers and clock gives 41.7%. Among touches that hit a barrier: 50.2% [49.5, 51.0] vs exactly 50% for the random walk. 2:1: 32.7% vs 32.8%. 1:2: 67.8% vs 67.2%.", "Real touches time out more than the random walk says (23% vs about 17% at 2 hours), on both sides equally. That is a vol shape effect (the average variance is inflated by bursts), not a direction effect.", "Geometry alone gives AUC well above 0.5: pooling the six shapes 0.69 on a pure random walk, minutes left in the day 0.59. The purged 6-fold logistic reaches AUC 0.573 on real labels and 0.568 on random-walk labels run at each day's actual vol. Brier skill: +1.3% vs the base rate, -0.45% vs the geometry alone.", "Target vs stop barely differ on any entry feature (gaps of 0.04σ-units or less); time-outs differ a lot (late, quiet, slow approach). A meta-model trained on target-first learns 'will this resolve', not 'which side wins'.", "After one median spread (0.035σ) every quintile of the model's P loses about -0.03 to -0.05σ per trade, the top quintile most; taking every touch -0.041σ, a random 20% -0.040σ. To pay, the 1:1 2-hour fade needs +4.3pp over the random walk; 0.25σ held to 21:00 needs about +7pp.", "Trades overlap: mean uniqueness 0.35, and the date-block variance is 3.5x the independent figure, so 60k touches are about 17k effective. Seeing 50% -> 53% needs 2,178 kept independent trades (5,186 after 100 trials), about 7,600 raw kept touches here.", "Stable by year: the real-minus-random-walk gap is negative every year 2016-2022 (2h fade -1.6 to -5.7pp, all time-out driven). Only EURUSD and EURCHF sit above the random walk (+1.1pp each); crosses are lowest."], "charts": [{"type": "groups", "title": "Fade the 0.5σ line: how often the target comes first, real vs a random walk", "names": ["Real (fade)", "Random walk, same barriers and clock"], "unit": "share of touches", "note": "Target first = 1, stop or time-out = 0. The random walk uses each touch's own barriers, its own minutes left and the instrument's average variance by time of day. The barrier shape sets almost the whole number; read the gap between the two dots, not their height.", "rows": [{"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h", "values": [0.3857, 0.4168]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, to 21:00", "values": [0.497, 0.4978]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, 2h", "values": [0.1495, 0.1629]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, to 21:00", "values": [0.426, 0.4608]}, {"label": "2:1 0.5/0.25σ, to 21:00", "values": [0.3075, 0.3223]}, {"label": "1:2 0.25/0.5σ, to 21:00", "values": [0.6421, 0.6553]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Real minus random walk, every shape and side, with the gap a trade must clear", "unit": "share of touches (0 = random walk)", "ref": 0, "note": "95% date-block intervals. In brackets: how far above the random walk the hit rate must sit just to pay the median spread and what time-outs returned. A filter has to find trades that clear that bracket, not trades above 0.", "rows": [{"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h fade (break-even +4.2pp)", "value": -0.0312, "lo": -0.0381, "hi": -0.0238}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h follow (break-even +5.0pp)", "value": -0.0351, "lo": -0.0426, "hi": -0.0277}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, to 21:00 fade (break-even +7.3pp)", "value": -0.0008, "lo": -0.0069, "hi": 0.0053}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, to 21:00 follow (break-even +7.4pp)", "value": -0.0121, "lo": -0.0184, "hi": -0.0057}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, 2h fade (break-even +2.5pp)", "value": -0.0134, "lo": -0.0184, "hi": -0.0081}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, 2h follow (break-even +4.3pp)", "value": 0.0018, "lo": -0.005, "hi": 0.0089}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, to 21:00 fade (break-even +0.3pp)", "value": -0.0349, "lo": -0.041, "hi": -0.0281}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, to 21:00 follow (break-even +0.5pp)", "value": -0.0366, "lo": -0.0428, "hi": -0.0306}, {"label": "2:1 0.5/0.25σ, to 21:00 fade (break-even +3.5pp)", "value": -0.0148, "lo": -0.0195, "hi": -0.0096}, {"label": "2:1 0.5/0.25σ, to 21:00 follow (break-even +3.9pp)", "value": -0.0172, "lo": -0.0223, "hi": -0.0117}, {"label": "1:2 0.25/0.5σ, to 21:00 fade (break-even +3.6pp)", "value": -0.0132, "lo": -0.0186, "hi": -0.0072}, {"label": "1:2 0.25/0.5σ, to 21:00 follow (break-even +3.4pp)", "value": -0.0215, "lo": -0.0272, "hi": -0.016}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Only the touches that hit a barrier: real vs b/(a+b)", "names": ["Real", "Random walk"], "unit": "P(target | a barrier was hit)", "note": "Without the time-outs a driftless walk gives about b/(a+b): 0.5 for 1:1, 0.33 for 2:1, 0.67 for 1:2 (time limits shift it a little). Fade and follow are mirrors, so their gaps have opposite signs. Fade above the random walk = touches tend to come back.", "rows": [{"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h fade", "values": [0.502, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h follow", "values": [0.4969, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, to 21:00 fade", "values": [0.5052, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, to 21:00 follow", "values": [0.4938, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, 2h fade", "values": [0.4754, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, 2h follow", "values": [0.524, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, to 21:00 fade", "values": [0.5008, 0.5]}, {"label": "1:1 0.5σ, to 21:00 follow", "values": [0.4988, 0.5]}, {"label": "2:1 0.5/0.25σ, to 21:00 fade", "values": [0.3265, 0.3284]}, {"label": "2:1 0.5/0.25σ, to 21:00 follow", "values": [0.322, 0.3284]}, {"label": "1:2 0.25/0.5σ, to 21:00 fade", "values": [0.6777, 0.6716]}, {"label": "1:2 0.25/0.5σ, to 21:00 follow", "values": [0.673, 0.6716]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "AUC above 0.5 with no edge at all: what geometry alone gives", "names": ["Pure random walk", "Real fade trades"], "unit": "ROC AUC (0.5 = no sorting)", "note": "Each score is ranked against the label it would face. On a random walk there is no direction to find, yet mixing barrier shapes, minutes left in the day, or the day's own vol all sort trades. A meta-model must beat these numbers, not 0.5. 'Vol so far' is scored against a random walk run at each day's actual vol.", "rows": [{"label": "6 barrier shapes pooled, score = b/(a+b) with time", "values": [0.6879, 0.6941]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h: score = geometry P (minutes left)", "values": [0.5917, 0.5857]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h: score = earlier entry", "values": [0.4485, 0.4647]}, {"label": "1:1 0.25σ, 2h: score = vol so far today", "values": [0.5274, 0.5284]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Each entry feature on its own (1:1 0.25σ, 2h, fade)", "names": ["Real trades", "Random walk at the day's vol"], "unit": "ROC AUC", "note": "Above 0.5: higher values go with the target. Where the real bar matches the random-walk bar, the feature is reading vol or time, not direction. Direction information would show as a real bar that differs from its random-walk twin.", "rows": [{"label": "time of day", "values": [0.5353, 0.5276]}, {"label": "went the other way first", "values": [0.5529, 0.5457]}, {"label": "move in last 15 min", "values": [0.5576, 0.5581]}, {"label": "move in last 60 min", "values": [0.5474, 0.5504]}, {"label": "vol so far vs last 20 days", "values": [0.5284, 0.5274]}, {"label": "sigma vs its 1-year median", "values": [0.4901, 0.4816]}, {"label": "yesterday's range vs sigma", "values": [0.5319, 0.5174]}, {"label": "|gap| at the open", "values": [0.4976, 0.5051]}, {"label": "spread at entry", "values": [0.5151, 0.514]}, {"label": "event day", "values": [0.5033, 0.499]}, {"label": "Monday", "values": [0.4861, 0.4913]}, {"label": "Friday", "values": [0.5045, 0.5003]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "How far apart the outcomes sit on each entry feature (1:1 0.25σ, 2h, fade)", "names": ["Target first minus stop first", "Time ran out minus stop first"], "unit": "standard deviations", "note": "Benchmark: 0 (a feature that knows nothing about the outcome). The target-vs-stop gap is all a filter could use to pick a side's winners; the time-out gap is mostly clock and vol (late, quiet touches run out of time).", "rows": [{"label": "time of day", "values": [-0.0062, -0.3563]}, {"label": "went the other way first", "values": [0.0041, -0.3966]}, {"label": "move in last 15 min", "values": [-0.0228, -0.4849]}, {"label": "move in last 60 min", "values": [-0.0213, -0.4642]}, {"label": "vol so far vs last 20 days", "values": [0.0057, -0.2433]}, {"label": "sigma vs its 1-year median", "values": [0.0406, 0.1975]}, {"label": "yesterday's range vs sigma", "values": [0.0447, -0.1635]}, {"label": "|gap| at the open", "values": [-0.0197, -0.0784]}, {"label": "spread at entry", "values": [0.0104, -0.1279]}]}, {"type": "hist", "title": "Label overlap: average uniqueness of each trade (1:1 0.25σ, 2h)", "unit": "uniqueness (1 = no other trade open at the same time)", "note": "AFML ch.4: uniqueness = mean over the trade's life of 1/(trades open). Mean 0.35, so 60,211 trades carry about 20,825 trades' worth of separate time. The date-block bootstrap says the hit rate's variance is 3.5x the independent-coin figure, an effective 17,167 trades. Benchmark: 1.0 for every trade if none overlapped.", "bins": [[0.0, 1485], [0.1, 17163], [0.2, 15306], [0.3, 9211], [0.4, 4825], [0.5, 4286], [0.6, 1840], [0.7, 1435], [0.8, 1159], [0.9, 3499]]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Power: retained trades needed to see a 50% hit rate become 50% + d", "unit": "trades kept by the filter", "xlabel": "lift in percentage points", "note": "80% power. 50 to 53% needs 2,178 independent kept trades at a single 5% test. Our trades are not independent: multiply by the design effect. A filter that keeps half of 60,211 touches keeps 30,105 raw, about 8,583 effective.", "series": [{"name": "5% test", "points": [[1, 19620], [2, 4903], [3, 2178], [4, 1224], [5, 783], [6, 543], [8, 304], [10, 194]]}, {"name": "Bonferroni over 100 trials", "points": [[1, 46704], [2, 11673], [3, 5186], [4, 2916], [5, 1865], [6, 1294], [8, 726], [10, 463]]}, {"name": "5% test x design effect 3.5", "points": [[1, 68815], [2, 17197], [3, 7639], [4, 4293], [5, 2746], [6, 1905], [8, 1066], [10, 680]]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Learning curve: logistic meta-model, last sixth of the window held out", "unit": "ROC AUC on the held-out block", "xlabel": "training trades", "note": "Purged by date with a 5-session embargo; 5 seeded subsamples per size. The random-walk line is the same model trained and scored on random-walk labels at each day's vol: what geometry and vol alone are worth. Real above random-walk = direction information. (1:1 0.25σ, 2h, fade)", "series": [{"name": "Real labels", "points": [[250, 0.537], [500, 0.5364], [1000, 0.5466], [2000, 0.553], [5000, 0.5611], [10000, 0.5642], [20000, 0.5651], [40000, 0.5672]]}, {"name": "Random walk at the day's vol", "points": [[250, 0.5304], [500, 0.5374], [1000, 0.5462], [2000, 0.559], [5000, 0.5665], [10000, 0.5717], [20000, 0.5723], [40000, 0.5734]]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Calibration: purged 6-fold logistic vs the random-walk geometry", "unit": "share that hit the target", "xlabel": "predicted P(target first)", "note": "Deciles of the out-of-fold prediction. On the diagonal = calibrated. AUC 0.573 (geometry alone 0.586). Brier skill vs the base rate 1.33%, vs the geometry -0.45%. Looked at only: the model was fitted on the same window and nothing was chosen from it. (1:1 0.25σ, 2h, fade)", "series": [{"name": "Logistic, out of fold", "points": [[0.2941, 0.2488], [0.3265, 0.3127], [0.3439, 0.3506], [0.3585, 0.3684], [0.3721, 0.3958], [0.386, 0.4225], [0.4012, 0.4267], [0.4194, 0.4332], [0.4439, 0.4405], [0.505, 0.4576]]}